<h1>Disclosure</h1>
<p>Amazon Associates links are <strong>on</strong> (<code>affiliates_enabled: {{ site.affiliates_enabled }}</code>). There are no ads. Nobody pays to be on, or kept off, this site, and no automaker or dealer has seen these pages before publication.</p>
<p>Model-year pages, and some component pages, can show a Parts and tools block. Each link goes straight to an Amazon search for a part or a diagnostic tool related to a component group owners named. The link uses <code>rel="sponsored"</code>. It does not show an Amazon price, rating, or image. A link is not a repair recommendation, and buying a part does not fix a recall. Recall repairs are free at a dealer.</p>
<p>Each model-year page also has one text link to the EpicVIN homepage for a vehicle history report. EpicVIN pays a commission on report purchases. That link has no banner and no price. Details are on the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.</p>
<p>The numbers on a page never depend on whether a link pays. Complaint and recall counts come only from NHTSA's data (see <a href="/about/">method</a> and the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>).</p>
